#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Static Windows prank lock screen -- "BossDefender".

This is the Windows counterpart of fake_noanime_ransom.py.  It paints one
frozen horror scene (no video, no continuous animation) over every monitor
and swallows every key except letters, digits, Shift, Enter and Backspace.

The passphrase is ``bomboclat``.  Type it and press Enter to unlock.

Only Windows is supported.  Ctrl+Alt+Del is the Windows secure-attention
sequence and cannot be intercepted by a normal application (the C# version
has the same limitation).  Keys handled entirely by keyboard firmware, such
as some Fn brightness keys, may never reach Windows and cannot be blocked by
a user-mode hook.

The prank fails closed: if its low-level keyboard or mouse hook cannot be
installed, it refuses to show the lock screen instead of running in a
half-protected state.  While it runs, the Shift/NumLock accessibility-hotkey
activation bits (Sticky Keys, Filter Keys and Toggle Keys) are temporarily
turned off so five quick Shift taps or a long right-Shift hold cannot open a
Windows accessibility shortcut.  The previous values are restored on exit.

Test aids::

    python fake_static_ransom_win.py --selftest
    python fake_static_ransom_win.py --windowed 1280x720 --duration 8
    python fake_static_ransom_win.py --windowed 1280x720 --autotype bomboclat --autotype-enter
    python fake_static_ransom_win.py --windowed 1280x720 --autotype nope --autotype-enter --duration 8
"""

